{"en":[{"partOfSpeech":"Noun","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":""},{"definition":"An <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/animal\" title=\"animal\">animal</a> of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/clade\" title=\"clade\">clade</a> (traditionally <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/class\" title=\"class\">class</a>) <span class=\"biota\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Aves#Translingual\" title=\"Aves\">Aves</a></span> in the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/phylum\" title=\"phylum\">phylum</a> <span class=\"biota\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Chordata#Translingual\" title=\"Chordata\">Chordata</a></span>, characterized by being warm-blooded, having <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/feather\" title=\"feather\">feathers</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/wing\" title=\"wing\">wings</a> usually capable of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/flight\" title=\"flight\">flight</a>, having a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/beak\" title=\"beak\">beaked</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/mouth\" title=\"mouth\">mouth</a>, and laying <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/egg\" title=\"egg\">eggs</a>.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"Ducks and sparrows are <b>birds</b>."}],"examples":["Ducks and sparrows are <b>birds</b>."]},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt51\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> Any winged <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/animal\" title=\"animal\">animal</a>."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt52\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> A young bird, a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/nestling\" title=\"nestling\">nestling</a>."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt55\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> A <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/man\" title=\"man\">man</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/fellow\" title=\"fellow\">fellow</a>. <style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r90144991\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/template